; Practical help guides. Shortcut assignments live in Keybindings.
class ModuleHelp {
    static Introduction(id) {
        switch id {
            case "window-cascade":
                return "GETTING STARTED"
                    . "`r`nNew application windows are arranged into cascading slots on your monitors. "
                    . "Open a few windows to see how slots and stacked windows work. "
                    . "Focus tabs and Keybindings let you select, rotate or swap visible windows."
                    . "`r`n`r`nWINDOW PLACEMENT"
                    . "`r`nMove windows between monitors or gather cascades onto one display. "
                    . "Pause automatic placement in Settings when new windows should stay put. "
                    . "Existing cascade controls continue working while placement is paused."
                    . "`r`n`r`nWORKING WITH WONDER WINDOWS"
                    . "`r`nA manually positioned window stays out of automatic cascading until "
                    . "you explicitly adopt or re-slot it. Focusing a window does not adopt it."
                    . "`r`n`r`nSettings controls focus tabs, colors and automatic placement. "
                    . "Use Keybindings to discover or customize your shortcuts."
            case "win-key-overhaul":
                return "GETTING STARTED"
                    . "`r`nWonder Windows arranges and navigates application windows manually. "
                    . "Try the left and right layout actions to cycle through several positions. "
                    . "Stretch windows toward neighbors, swap positions or change focus. "
                    . "Maximize cycles between a maximized window and borderless fullscreen."
                    . "`r`n`r`nWORKING WITH CASCADE KINGDOM"
                    . "`r`nManual placement takes precedence over automatic cascading until you "
                    . "choose to re-adopt the window in Cascade Kingdom. "
                    . "Paper Pad has its own page navigation when its editor is focused."
                    . "`r`n`r`nCOMPATIBILITY"
                    . "`r`nWindows Snap, ScreenGrid and FancyZones may overlap with these controls. "
                    . "Settings explains the compatibility options and asks before making changes. "
                    . "Use Keybindings to inspect or customize the available actions."
            case "power-hotkey":
                return "GETTING STARTED"
                    . "`r`nPower-Up Utilities adds keyboard outputs, text tools and system actions. "
                    . "Assign F13-F24 or virtual number-pad outputs in Keybindings. "
                    . "Text actions insert symbols or a yyyyMMdd-HHmmss timestamp."
                    . "`r`n`r`nWHERE COMMANDS WORK"
                    . "`r`nWindows Terminal commands work only in Windows Terminal. "
                    . "Sleep and speaker-wake actions affect the computer. "
                    . "Held virtual keys are released when you release their trigger. "
                    . "Text and system actions wait until trigger keys are released."
                    . "`r`n`r`nCUSTOMIZING"
                    . "`r`nUse Keybindings to assign or clear shortcuts. "
                    . "There is no separate Power-Up Utilities editor or settings page."
            case "scratchpad":
                return "GETTING STARTED"
                    . "`r`nPaper Pad uses a dedicated Notepad3 window for quick notes. "
                    . "Choose Open Pad below, or assign a shortcut to toggle the window. "
                    . "Create new pages, switch between them and save ordinary files. "
                    . "Editor-only shortcuts affect Paper Pad, not your other applications."
                    . "`r`n`r`nSAVING AND CLOSING"
                    . "`r`nPaper Pad checks unsaved changes before hiding, switching pages or exiting. "
                    . "Save As can rename a page within the notes folder. "
                    . "Undo survives hiding but not switching pages. "
                    . "Resolve pending Notepad3 dialogs before retrying a save or restart."
                    . "`r`n`r`nCUSTOMIZING"
                    . "`r`nSettings controls the notes folder, editor path, display and autosave. "
                    . "Changing paths never moves or deletes your existing notes."
            case "keyboard-layers":
                return "GETTING STARTED"
                    . "`r`nSecret Keys turns CapsLock and Pause into optional shortcut layers. "
                    . "Hold either key and press another key to trigger its assigned action. "
                    . "Or briefly tap the key to arm the next key for 1.4 seconds. "
                    . "Tap again to cancel. The two layers do not stack. "
                    . "An unassigned key cancels the one-shot shortcut and passes through."
                    . "`r`n`r`nENABLING AND DISABLING"
                    . "`r`nSettings lets you turn CapsLock and Pause layers off independently. "
                    . "Modules contains the master switch for Secret Keys. "
                    . "A disabled layer restores its physical key unless you reassign it. "
                    . "Saved shortcuts remain editable in Keybindings."
                    . "`r`n`r`nThe default Ctrl + Alt + K still opens Keybindings when both "
                    . "layers are disabled, unless you have reassigned that shortcut."
        }
        return ""
    }

    static Text(id, manager) => this.Introduction(id)
}
